commit ec963d3efbc33d9ee2d38e47b29c4aeedb76986f

C03: asking what is on the screen or to describe it reads its text and says images are out of reach (SCREEN1417)

«qué hay en la pantalla» (H0164), «describime la pantalla» (H0564), «leé la pantalla» (H0716) and the forms «qué ves en mi pantalla», «describe lo que ves», «leeme la pantalla» reached no reader: the implicit screen reading required a read verb plus an object noun, and the describe forms pointed at vision.describe, which needs a vision provider (HTTPS endpoint and model) that this PC does not have.

effect_intent: a bare «leé/leeme/read (la|mi|the|my) pantalla|screen» and the screen-content questions and describe forms («qué hay/se ve/aparece/ves/estás viendo en (mi|la) pantalla», «describime/describe/describí la pantalla | lo que ves», «what do you see on my screen», «describe what you see») resolve to capture.screenshot + ocr.read; the phone/car and «cómo puedo» exclusions keep applying; the speech-act gate accepts describime/describeme/describí/describila.
llm.compose_user_message: when the request asked what is on the screen or to describe it, the reading instruction says first that images cannot be described, only the screen text read, then reports the lines; the grounding stoplist is reduced to reading, position and connective words so invented interface descriptions («una ventana de configuración del sistema») are vetoed.

No .NET change. Offline probe: fourteen forms resolve, nine boundaries stay inert, grounded drafts pass, three invented descriptions are vetoed. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


